# InstallTool.action
#
# The ROS2-action form of problog_project's InstallTool BT node (see
# module/contracts/schema.yaml's own InstallTool entry). An action, not
# a service like TakeSample, because it's DURATIVE -- same start/halt
# shape as MoveTo.action, a fixed-Duration analogue of one
# startMoveto/haltMoveto pair, just without the continuous trajectory
# (the robot never moves during this action).
#
# Server: amiga_ros2_planners' tool_action_node, which runs this for
# `tool`'s own configured Duration (this problem's own config.yaml,
# tool.install.duration_seconds.<tool>), resolving a success/failure
# coin flip (tool.install.success_probability) once the full Duration
# elapses, or halting early if an always-on safety cutoff trips
# (battery depleted / collision detected -- safety_monitor.py). On
# success, tool_action_node updates its own tracked "currently equipped
# tool" state (published on the latched `tool_state` topic) -- see
# move_to_node.py's own note on how that changes a SUBSEQUENT MoveTo's
# speed, and battery_sim_node's own note on how it changes
# moving_drain_rate. Only takes the input needed to execute: no
# triggers/reason port, and the result reports only success/failure
# (see `status` below), not why.

# "cart" or "plow" -- the ONLY two tool kinds accepted.
string tool
---
# Result

# true iff the full Duration elapsed AND the coin flip succeeded --
# false for anything else (a failed coin flip, a safety cutoff, a
# cancel, a precondition failure).
bool status
---
# Feedback

# Wall-clock seconds elapsed since this action started.
float64 elapsed_s
